# 🔌 7. Ports

## Format

```text
-p HOST_PORT:CONTAINER_PORT
```

Example:

```bash
docker run -d \
  --name app01 \
  -p 9090:8080 \
  myapp:v1
```

Flow:

```text
Browser
   │
   ▼
SERVER :9090
   │
   ▼
CONTAINER :8080
   │
   ▼
Application
```

Test:

```bash
curl -i http://localhost:9090
```

Check published ports:

```bash
docker ps
```

or:

```bash
docker port app01
```

### ⭐ EXPOSE vs `-p`

Dockerfile:

```dockerfile
EXPOSE 8080
```

Runtime:

```bash
docker run -p 9090:8080 myapp:v1
```

| Setting | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `EXPOSE 8080` | Documents container port |
| `-p 9090:8080` | Actually publishes port |

> 🧠 **EXPOSE does not publish a port.**

