# 💾 9. Docker Storage

Three important types:

```text
1. Named Volume
2. Bind Mount
3. Anonymous Volume
```

---

## 🟢 Named Volume

Create:

```bash
docker volume create app-data
```

Use:

```bash
docker run -d \
  --name app01 \
  -v app-data:/data \
  myapp:v1
```

Format:

```text
VOLUME_NAME:CONTAINER_PATH

app-data:/data
```

Docker manages the host-side location.

### Check

```bash
docker volume ls
docker volume inspect app-data
```

---

## 🔵 Bind Mount

```bash
docker run -d \
  --name app01 \
  -v /home/ubuntu/app-data:/data \
  myapp:v1
```

Format:

```text
HOST_PATH:CONTAINER_PATH
```

Example:

```text
/home/ubuntu/app-data:/data
```

Read-only:

```bash
docker run -d \
  -v /home/ubuntu/config:/config:ro \
  myapp:v1
```

---

## 🟡 Anonymous Volume

```bash
docker run -d \
  -v /data \
  myapp:v1
```

Docker generates the volume name.

---

## ⭐ Storage Memory Trick

| Type | Example | Managed By |
|---|---|---|
| Named Volume | `app-data:/data` | Docker |
| Bind Mount | `/opt/data:/data` | Us |
| Anonymous | `/data` | Docker-generated |

```text
Named Volume
app-data:/data

Bind Mount
/host/path:/container/path
```

