# ❤️ 13. Healthcheck

Dockerfile example:

```dockerfile
HEALTHCHECK \
  --interval=10s \
  --timeout=3s \
  --retries=3 \
  CMD curl -f http://localhost:8080/health || exit 1
```

Meaning:

```text
Check every 10 sec
       ↓
Timeout after 3 sec
       ↓
3 consecutive failures
       ↓
UNHEALTHY
```

Check:

```bash
docker ps
```

Detailed:

```bash
docker inspect \
  -f '{{json .State.Health}}' \
  app01
```

Possible states:

```text
starting
healthy
unhealthy
```

### ⭐ Important

```text
UP ≠ HEALTHY
```

Example:

```text
Up 10 minutes (unhealthy)
```

means:

```text
Main process → running
Healthcheck  → failing
```

> ⚠️ A bad healthcheck can mark a working application as unhealthy.

> ⚠️ Standalone Docker does not automatically restart a container merely because its health status becomes `unhealthy`.

