docker inspect \
  -f '{{.State.OOMKilled}}' \
  app01
```

Command:

```bash
docker inspect \
  -f '{{json .Config.Cmd}}' \
  app01
```

---

# 🌐 35. Website Not Opening

Check container:

```bash
docker ps
```

Check port:

```bash
docker port app01
```

Logs:

```bash
docker logs --tail 100 app01
```

Test from host:

```bash
curl -i http://localhost:9090
```

Check port configuration:

```bash
docker inspect \
  -f '{{json .NetworkSettings.Ports}}' \
  app01
```

Remember:

```text
-p 9090:8080
```

means:

```text
HOST 9090
   ↓
CONTAINER 8080
```

It does **not** guarantee the application is actually listening on `8080`.

---

# 🌍 36. Network / DNS Problem

List:

```bash
docker network ls
```

Inspect:

```bash
docker network inspect app-network
```

Check container networks:

```bash
docker inspect \
  -f '{{json .NetworkSettings.Networks}}' \
  app01
```

From another container on the same user-defined network, use:

```text
app01:8080
```

rather than depending on a container IP.

---

# 👤 37. Permission Problem

Check runtime user:

```bash
docker exec app01 whoami
```

Check directory:

```bash
docker exec app01 ls -ld /app
```

Inspect configured user:

```bash
docker inspect \
  -f '{{.Config.User}}' \
  app01
```

Possible Dockerfile pattern:

```dockerfile
RUN chown -R appuser:appuser /app
USER appuser
```

---

# 💾 38. Data / Mount Problem

Check mounts:

```bash
docker inspect \
  -f '{{json .Mounts}}' \
  app01
```

Volumes:

```bash
docker volume ls
```

Inspect volume:

```bash
docker volume inspect app-data
```

Remember:

```text
Container filesystem
      ↓ removed container
Data may disappear


Volume
      ↓ removed container
Data can persist
```

---

# ❤️ 39. Health Problem

Check:

```bash
docker ps
```

Detailed:

```bash
docker inspect \
  -f '{{json .State.Health}}' \
  app01
```

Then verify the same endpoint manually where appropriate:

```bash
curl -i http://localhost:9090/health
```

Remember:

```text
Container running
      ≠
Application healthy
```

